## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design a multi-tenant streaming data platform on GCP that enforces schema contracts, detects drift in real time, and implements automated remediation—all while balancing latency and cost considerations.

## Key Concepts

- **Data Contracts in Data Catalog**: Registering and managing versioned schemas per tenant to enforce contract compliance
- **Drift Detection in Streaming Pipelines**: Real-time identification of schema changes from source systems against canonical schemas
- **Canonical vs Source Schemas**: Transforming heterogeneous source formats into a unified Parquet schema
- **BigLake External Tables**: Enabling per-tenant secure views over shared data with access controls
- **Versioned Schema Management and Rollback**: Maintaining schema history and implementing safe rollbacks when contract violations occur
- **Data Quality Observability and Alerting**: Monitoring pipeline health and triggering alerts on drift detection
- **BigQuery Time Travel**: Using temporal tables for backfill and recovery operations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: drift check between source and canonical schemas
function checkDrift(sourceSchema, canonicalSchema) {
  const drift = {
    added: [],
    removed: [],
    typeChanged: []
  };

  for (const field of sourceSchema.fields) {
    const canonicalField = canonicalSchema.fields[field.name];
    if (!canonicalField) {
      drift.added.push(field);
    } else if (field.type !== canonicalField.type) {
      drift.typeChanged.push({ field: field.name, expected: canonicalField.type, actual: field.type });
    }
  }

  for (const field of canonicalSchema.fields) {
    if (!sourceSchema.fields[field.name]) {
      drift.removed.push(field);
    }
  }

  return drift;
}

// Alert on drift detection
function handleDrift(drift, tenantId) {
  if (drift.added.length > 0 || drift.removed.length > 0 || drift.typeChanged.length > 0) {
    sendAlert({
      tenantId,
      severity: 'HIGH',
      message: `Schema drift detected: ${JSON.stringify(drift)}`,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
    });
    pausePipeline(tenantId);
  }
}
```
